# DAILY DEVELOPMENT REPORT

**Date:** 10 July 2026
**Developer:** Ian Macharia
**Project:** YohPal Live

## 1. Completed Today

* Reviewed the Release 1.0 patch documents (1.0A–1.0E, starter pack, Executive Verdict) against the current codebase, corrected several assumptions in them against real file paths and collections, and produced an implementation plan splitting the work into parallel tracks.
* Implemented Release Track 1.0B — Money, Security & Wallet Reconciliation, in full:
  * Added a server-validated gift purchase flow (`validatedGiftPurchase` Cloud Function) that checks a real price catalog and debits the sender's wallet balance before crediting a creator — closing the "client sets its own gift amount" fraud gap.
  * Added elapsed-time verification to rewarded-ad crediting (`rewardedAdProcessor`) plus a `verifyRewardedAd` callable, mitigating spoofed ad-reward claims.
  * Hardened Firestore rules for `gifts`, `videoStats`, `referralEvents`, and `liveSessions` so client writes can no longer set arbitrary values or edit other users' data.
  * Replaced the unbuilt `WalletStatusScreen` placeholder with a real screen and a `yohpal://wallet-status` deep link, so users get feedback after returning from a wallet top-up/withdrawal on YohPal Web.
  * Found and fixed a live backend bug: the M-Pesa payout function was reading/writing a `wallets` collection nothing else in the codebase populated, so every payout request failed "insufficient balance" regardless of actual balance.
* Implemented and wired sign-out end to end (confirm dialog, loading state, correct navigation back to the login screen) — previously fully coded but unreachable from any screen.
* Implemented real Google and Apple Sign-In (native credential exchange via Firebase, not stubs), including iOS URL scheme and Apple Sign In entitlement configuration, and platform-appropriate hiding of Apple's option on Android.
* Caught and fixed a regression introduced by the SSO work: Google sign-out was blocking the underlying Firebase sign-out on failure, which broke logout for any user who had never used Google Sign-In.
* Redesigned the login and signup screens: removed the boxed card layout, added the brand mark, restyled the form fields, added a "Forgot password" entry point (stubbed), an "or continue with" divider, and the Google/Apple sign-in tiles.
* Added a required Terms & Conditions acceptance step to signup, including a real Terms & Conditions screen, plus a confirm-password field and a first/last name split on the signup form.
* Wrote a full implementation status report re-verifying the codebase against every Critical/High/Medium/Low finding in the Production Readiness Review, published as both an HTML artifact and a PDF in `docs/`.

